{
    "word": "accouterment",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                "word": "accouterment",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c4e443fa-2275-4025-a564-9687ee3763af",
                        "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "accouterments"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dff669ab-c557-3bbf-bc7c-3a417fb99ad3",
                        "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A soldier's equipment, other than weapons and uniform."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb8b9996-b5e3-4e39-bb09-898ff0b8cac9",
                                "sense_id": "dff669ab-c557-3bbf-bc7c-3a417fb99ad3",
                                "text": "Thus One / Jovial his Mate bespoke; O Friend, observe, / How gay with all th'Accoutrements of War / The Britons come, with Gold well fraught they come"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32707aa5-b749-45e9-b047-a26976d309cb",
                                "sense_id": "dff669ab-c557-3bbf-bc7c-3a417fb99ad3",
                                "text": "Three thousand six hundred of the best fighting men, with complete accoutrement; with cannoneers even, and cannon!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdf2fc43-93a9-4ba6-b8e6-71533063191c",
                                "sense_id": "dff669ab-c557-3bbf-bc7c-3a417fb99ad3",
                                "text": "He [Manolo] was supposed to have left Spain while he was doing his military service, that is to say he was in the cavalry and he went across the border, and sold his horse and his accoutrement, and so had enough money to come to Paris and be a sculptor."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                        "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An article of clothing or equipment, in particular when used as an accessory."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bc6fa09-3884-4f2f-aa65-6f4d6760a5e8",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "To me ſhe's married, not vnto my cloathes: / Could I repaire what ſhe will weare in me, / As I can change theſe poore accoutrements, / 'Twere well for Kate, and better for my ſelfe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78d7e646-18c9-48bb-91a9-6812437e656a",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "While one of these loiterers showed the red skin and wild accouterments of a native of the woods, the other exhibited, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "575513cb-99cc-47c5-b0c1-062000b853fe",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "And then from beyond the blank wall beside which I lay I heard the shuffling of feet, the snarling of grim beasts, the clank of metal accouterments, and the heavy breathing of a man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4d27452-fdeb-4f2c-b7a7-0fdb66e347e1",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "An essential accoutrement to participation in the daily grind of New York is a briefcase, and any self-respecting office slave eventually amasses a collection, from canvas bags to stylish leather-covered boxes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "538cb879-8fe2-448b-b3d2-43becb07cbdc",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "They used rock'n'roll as a weapon against itself. With all instruments but guitar, bass, drums, and voice written off as effete, as elitist accoutrements of a professionalist cult of technique, it was music best suited to anger and frustration, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b365ccd2-634e-4b01-a0fb-f3742351c82b",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "Partly for this reason, the washing machine–like dishwashers after the mid-1970s–remained associated in commercial imagery with the domestic accoutrements of the affluent middle class."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ece6152-e9bf-4f64-b947-5aee6c23bb87",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "It took me a second to identify what they were selling: accoutrements of mourning and/or ancestral worship. Spirit money, yellow bills imprinted with gold foil, was tied with red string and shrink-wrapped in thick stacks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b605674-10bd-4286-8a88-fb84a63c15a3",
                                "sense_id": "2cdfe7c3-6666-3269-929c-9b2bc52ef6e8",
                                "text": "Now that the face mask has become the essential accoutrement of our lives, the COVID pandemic has laid bare our fundamental need to see whole faces."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db23be07-a537-3d10-b609-ba8d197804d8",
                        "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An identifying yet superficial characteristic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb45d32f-d8b4-40db-aa28-6af01f0fd1d5",
                                "sense_id": "db23be07-a537-3d10-b609-ba8d197804d8",
                                "text": "By the summer of 1964 they had achieved the bigger house on the better street and the familiar accouterments of a family on its way up: the $30,000 a year, the three children for the Christmas card, the picture window, the family room, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bae3809-0dfe-4c95-8e5c-1f3ba7d34eee",
                                "sense_id": "db23be07-a537-3d10-b609-ba8d197804d8",
                                "text": "But musical ancestry aside, the influence to which [Justin] Bieber is most beholden is the current trends in pop music, which means Believe is loaded up with EDM accouterments, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3c7f425-cb1a-3d9a-973a-796efcb98cb2",
                        "entry_id": "62d8a5ef-b8fa-3b26-8071-2dfca5752097",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of accoutering; furnishing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
